<section>
  <h2>Housekeeping services</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Corporate housekeeping</strong> — Daily office cleaning, washroom upkeep, glass and floor maintenance, pantry coordination.</li>
    <li><strong>Industrial cleaning</strong> — Factory floors, machine surrounds, oil-spill management, hazardous-waste handling under supervision.</li>
    <li><strong>Hotel & resort housekeeping</strong> — Trained room attendants with hospitality grooming, linen and amenity management, public-area cleaning.</li>
    <li><strong>Hospital sanitation</strong> — Trained for biomedical-waste segregation, OPD cleaning, infection-control protocols (under your IPC team's supervision).</li>
    <li><strong>Deep cleaning</strong> — Quarterly or one-off deep cleans with chemical inventory and equipment.</li>
    <li><strong>Mall and retail housekeeping</strong> — High-traffic floor maintenance, restroom rotation, food-court cleanup.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Support staff</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Pantry and F&amp;B</strong> — Tea-coffee, plated lunch service, banquet support staff.</li>
    <li><strong>Maintenance teams</strong> — Liaison electricians, plumbers, AC technicians (we coordinate; specialised licensed work is contracted appropriately).</li>
    <li><strong>Drivers and transport pool</strong> — Verified, licensed drivers for executive transport and operational vehicles.</li>
    <li><strong>Gardening and landscape</strong> — Daily gardener for corporate campuses, hotels and townships.</li>
    <li><strong>Reception and front-office support</strong> — Trained reception staff, visitor management, courier handling.</li>
    <li><strong>Fire-safety attendants</strong> — Trained fire-watch staff for sites without a permanent fire-safety officer.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How combined contracts work</h2>
  <p>Most of our enterprise clients consolidate security and facility management on a single contract with us. This typically gives:</p>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>One supervisor as the single point of accountability across both teams.</li>
    <li>Cross-trained staff for low-traffic shifts (one fewer person on the roster, savings shared).</li>
    <li>Single monthly invoice with combined statutory compliance reporting.</li>
    <li>Negotiated discount on the combined contract vs. two separate vendors.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
